316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Thanksgiving is a national holiday that is rooted in a settler colonial history. But what does that mean? It is oftentimes associated with the Pilgrims and their harvest meal with the American indigenous peoples. This perspective not only ignores the rupturing traumas that indigenous peoples went through \(dispossession of their land, cultural erasure, and mass death\), but also fails to view the violence as a structure, as a paradigm for economic and state formation. The following articles discuss the term settler colonialism, providing a brief survey of its implications. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [40]
>>
endobj
